{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011Cf94VybyKce3MJGK4qCm2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! All tests pass successfully. Let me create a summary of the implementation:\n\n## Implementation Summary\n\nI've successfully implemented BE-005 with three major features:\n\n### 1. **Partial Fulfilment**\n- **Order quantities**: Orders and shipments now carry an optional `quantity` field (default 1). Quantities below 1 are rejected with HTTP 400.\n- **Allocation tracking**: `POST /shipments` validates that a new shipment won't exceed the order's quantity, rejecting with HTTP 409 if it would.\n- **Shipment transitions**: Added three new endpoints:\n  - `POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm` — CREATED → CONFIRMED\n  - `POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/deliver` — CONFIRMED → DELIVERED\n  - `POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/cancel` — CREATED → CANCELLED\n- **Fulfilment status**: Orders now report `fulfilment: { allocated, delivered, status }` where status is:\n  - `UNALLOCATED` — no shipments allocated\n  - `PARTIALLY_ALLOCATED` — some but not all quantity allocated\n  - `FULLY_ALLOCATED` — all quantity allocated but not delivered\n  - `DELIVERED` — all quantity delivered\n- **Quantity amendment**: `PUT /orders/{orderId}/quantity` updates an order's quantity with validation that it cannot go below the currently allocated quantity.\n- **Cancellation releases quantity**: Cancelled shipments don't count toward allocation, allowing their quantity to be re-allocated.\n\n### 2. **Customer Validation**\n- `POST /orders` now validates that the customer exists, rejecting with HTTP 422 if not.\n- `GET /customers/{customerId}` returns HTTP 404 through the standard error envelope (consistent with orders and shipments).\n\n### 3. **Paged Lists**\n- `GET /customers`, `GET /orders`, and `GET /shipments` now accept:\n  - `limit` (1-100, default 100) — items per page\n  - `offset` (0+, default 0) — starting position\n- All list responses include `X-Total-Count` header with the total count (before slicing, and after `fulfilment` filter for orders).\n- Invalid limit/offset values return HTTP 400 with field violation details.\n- `GET /orders?fulfilment=STATUS` filters orders by fulfilment status, rejecting unknown statuses with HTTP 400.\n\n### Changes Made\n\n**API Package** (`api/`):\n- Added `UnprocessableEntityException` for HTTP 422 responses\n- Added error codes: `CUSTOMER_NOT_FOUND`, `CUSTOMER_DOES_NOT_EXIST`, `ALLOCATION_EXCEEDS_QUANTITY`, `INVALID_SHIPMENT_TRANSITION`\n\n**Domain Entities**:\n- **Order.kt**: Added `quantity`, `Fulfilment` data class, `FulfilmentStatus` enum, `UpdateOrderQuantityRequest`\n- **Shipment.kt**: Added `quantity` field, `DELIVERED` status to enum\n\n**Controllers & Repositories**:\n- **OrderController**: Customer validation, fulfilment calculation, paging, quantity amendment, filter by status\n- **ShipmentController**: Quantity validation, allocation checking, shipment transitions, paging\n- **CustomerController**: Error envelope for 404, paging\n- All repositories: Added `findAllPaginated` and `PaginatedResult` support\n\n**Tests**:\n- Updated `OrderControllerTest` to create customers before creating orders\n- Enhanced `CustomerControllerTest` to verify error envelope\n\n### Acceptance Criteria Met ✓\n- ✓ Existing build passes\n- ✓ All tests pass (13 total)\n- ✓ Quantities, allocation, transitions, fulfilment status, and filtering work as specified\n- ✓ Error responses are consistent with the error envelope pattern\n- ✓ Customer validation and paging implemented correctly\n- ✓ No new Maven dependencies\n- ✓ No unrelated production file changes\n- ✓ Only modified order, shipment, customer features and shared api package"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2256,"cache_read_input_tokens":63629,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2256},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7513a2c6-539a-41b5-aba0-b1dd1a40fe16","uuid":"707d584e-5225-46f6-a375-f23645b5ecd7","timestamp":"2026-09-17T13:06:18.204Z","request_id":"req_011Cf94VyDeobhisxWDGPgpw"}
